        <h2>SEO in 2026: What Has Changed</h2>
        <p>SEO is not the same discipline it was five years ago. Several shifts in 2026 have changed how agencies approach optimization.</p>
        <p>AI-generated search results are now a permanent feature of Google. Search Generative Experience and AI overviews mean users sometimes get answers without clicking through to websites. This makes ranking in position one less valuable than being cited in the AI summary. Agencies now optimize for AI visibility, not just blue-link rankings.</p>
        <p>E-E-A-T signals — Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness — have become explicit ranking factors. Google wants to know who wrote your content, what credentials they have, and whether the information is accurate. Anonymous, generic content no longer performs well.</p>
        <p>Voice and conversational search continue growing. People ask Siri and Alexa full questions, not two-word keywords. Content must answer natural language queries directly and completely.</p>
        <p>Visual search is expanding. Google Lens and similar tools let users search with images. Image SEO — descriptive file names, alt text, and structured data — is now essential, not optional.</p>
        <p>Zero-click searches dominate many niches. Featured snippets, People Also Ask boxes, and knowledge panels answer queries directly on the search results page. SEO strategy must account for capturing these positions even when they do not drive clicks.</p>

        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About SEO Services</h2>

        <h3>What is included in SEO services?</h3>
        <p>SEO services typically include website audits, keyword research, on-page optimization, technical SEO fixes, content creation, link building, local SEO, and monthly reporting. The exact mix depends on your package and business needs.</p>

        <h3>How much should a small business spend on SEO?</h3>
        <p>Most small businesses should budget $1,500 to $3,500 per month for professional SEO. Budgets below $1,000 per month usually limit the scope too much to produce meaningful results in competitive markets.</p>

        <h3>Can I do SEO myself?</h3>
        <p>Yes, but it requires significant time and learning. DIY SEO works for businesses with marketing experience and 10 to 20 hours per week to dedicate. Most business owners get better results by hiring professionals. <a href="/blog/diy-seo-vs-hiring-an-agency-pros-and-cons/">See our full DIY vs agency comparison.</a></p>

        <h3>How do I know if SEO is working?</h3>
        <p>Track keyword rankings, organic traffic, and conversions month over month. A good agency provides transparent reporting that connects SEO activity to business outcomes like leads and revenue.</p>

        <h3>What is the difference between local SEO and national SEO?</h3>
        <p>Local SEO targets geographic-specific searches and Google Business Profile rankings. National SEO targets broader keywords without location modifiers. Local SEO is essential for service-area businesses. National SEO suits e-commerce and online brands. <a href="/blog/seo-for-local-businesses/">Learn more in our local SEO guide.</a></p>

        <h3>Will SEO work for my industry?</h3>
        <p>SEO works for nearly every industry that has search demand. The question is not whether SEO works — it is whether the search volume and competition in your niche justify the investment. A professional audit answers this question definitively.</p>

        <h3>What happens if I stop doing SEO?</h3>
        <p>Your rankings will not disappear overnight, but they will gradually decline as competitors continue optimizing. SEO is like fitness. Stopping does not erase past gains, but you lose ground over time.</p>

        <h3>How do I choose the right SEO company?</h3>
        <p>Look for transparent reporting, customized strategies, realistic timelines, and a track record in your industry. Avoid guarantees, instant results claims, and one-size-fits-all packages. Ask for case studies and references. <a href="/services/seo/">See how our SEO services work.</a></p>

        <p class="conclusion">SEO services are not a mystery. They are a system of interconnected disciplines that, when executed consistently, produce compounding returns. The businesses that win in search are not the ones that found a secret tactic. They are the ones that invested in the fundamentals — technical health, quality content, authoritative backlinks, and local presence — and stuck with it long enough for the results to materialize. If you are ready to stop guessing and start growing, the next step is a clear strategy built for your specific business.</p>

